Components go here.

This pack carries the runtime and no component: which component an appliance
runs is a deployment decision rather than a property of the runtime. A
component arrives from another pack whose overlay puts it at
/opt/components/hello.wasm, the path /etc/default/wasm-component names —
packs/hello-component is the worked example — and from then on its bytes are
in the solution hash, so "which logic shipped on which device" has an answer.

It must be a component, not a core module: wasmtime runs components under
WASI 0.2, and a core module built with wat2wasm is not one. Rust's
wasm32-wasip2 target produces a component directly.

The unit refuses to start without it rather than starting and doing nothing,
which is the same reasoning as the model placeholder in packs/inference.
